From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] lumaui: Sound › Volume mixer

Sound gains a Volume mixer page (sound-mixer): the default output, System
sounds and every app with a sound stream, each with its volume, a live
level, mute and (apps) the output it plays on.

Apps come from org.projectluma.AudioDevices1 version 2; the output uses
the sound adapter's GVC controls (vol and a new mute key). Outputs are
named by node name as the device rows name them (CFSINKS). The volume and
its level are LumaUI's LumaVolumeSlider with its LumaAudioMeter laid along
the track. A wide page draws one well of 96 px channel strips on a grid
that wraps at any width, the output first and raised; every strip's parts
sit on the same lines (two-line names). A phone or a TV draws rows, the
volume flat under the words with its track starting on their edge.
Levels are watched only while the page is mapped in a window that is not
suspended. The row replaces Volume by app in live mode while the service
offers version 2.
---
